---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../site.config';
import { paths } from '../lib/url';
---

<Base title="Privacy" description="What Football Stories 101 collects, which is very little, and why." path={paths.privacy()}>
  <div class="narrow prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p>This page is short because the publication collects almost nothing.</p>

    <h2>The website</h2>
    <p>
      The site is static. It sets no cookies, runs no advertising and loads no third-party share buttons or social
      widgets. Search runs entirely in your browser. If visitor statistics are ever switched on they will use a
      cookieless, privacy-respecting counter that stores no personal data, which is why there is no cookie banner.
    </p>

    <h2>The email list</h2>
    <p>
      When you subscribe, your email address is stored by Buttondown, the newsletter service that sends the daily story,
      together with the date you subscribed and, if you confirm by email, that confirmation. It is used for one purpose:
      sending you Football Stories 101. It is never sold, shared or used for anything else.
    </p>
    <p>
      Every email contains an unsubscribe link. Unsubscribing takes effect immediately in the mailing system, well within
      the ten business days required by Singapore's Personal Data Protection Act and Spam Control Act. You can also ask
      for your address to be deleted entirely by emailing <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Telegram and social media</h2>
    <p>
      The Telegram channel and the Facebook, Instagram and Threads accounts are run by their respective platforms under
      their own privacy policies. The publication sees only what those platforms show every page owner.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about this page, corrections or takedown requests: <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
